{
  "dom_id": "step-q556486",
  "name": "Question 20",
  "problem": "Estimate the value of $\\sqrt[3]{20},$ rounded to $1$ decimal place.\n\n$\\sqrt[3]{20}≈$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "To estimate $\\sqrt[3]{20},$ we first find the two perfect cubes closest to $20.$\n\nThe closest perfect cubes are $8={2}^{3}$ and $27={3}^{3}.$\n\nSince $8<20<27,$ we know that the cube root of $20$ lies between $2$ and $3.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14185481/assets/c4eb7ee1951d0d402df1553d46bc6e8ce1fdb421adc40949b9e79964484892c6.png)\n\nBecause $20$ is closer to $27$ than to $8,$ we expect $\\sqrt[3]{20}$ to be close to $3.$ \n\nLet's test a decimal near $3,$ such as $2.7,$ by cubing it:\n\n$$\n{2.7}^{3}=19.683\n$$\n\nSince $19.683$ is slightly less than $20,$ we know that $2.7<\\sqrt[3]{20}<2.8.$\n\nNext, we determine whether $20$ is closer to ${2.7}^{3}$ or ${2.8}^{3}:$\n\n- The distance from $20$ to ${2.7}^{3}$ is $20-19.683=0.317.$\n\n- The distance from $20$ to ${2.8}^{3}$ is $21.952-20=1.952.$\n\nSince $20$ is much closer to $19.683,$ $\\sqrt[3]{20}$ is closer to $2.7.$\n\nTherefore, rounded to $1$ decimal place, $\\sqrt[3]{20}≈2.7.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [
    {
